// ALERT (DIAAT-285, critical): service unavailable, endpoint availability.
//
// Measure: availability_pct per service (cloud_RoleName) and area over the alert window,
//   with the formula and exclusions of service_availability_endpoint.kql: 5xx and
//   no-status failures are unavailable, 4xx are available, health and version probes
//   and synthetic traffic excluded.
// Area: hmcts.area as transcribe-api sets it (empty: shared paths and transcribe-web),
//   so a failing area is visible even when the other is busy.
// Fires when availability_pct < the threshold (alert_thresholds.endpoint_availability_pct).
// Parameter (prepended by Terraform as a let): min_requests, so one failed request out
//   of two at night does not page anyone. Quiet periods are covered by the web tests.
// Output (AC3): the service name, the area, a count and a percentage. Nothing else.
// To run in Logs: prepend `let min_requests = 10;`.
requests
| where isempty(operation_SyntheticSource)
| where not(url matches regex @"(?i)/(health|healthz|healthcheck|livez|readyz|version)(/|\?|$)")
| extend area = tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.area"])
| extend status = toint(resultCode)
| summarize
    requests = sum(itemCount),
    unavailable = sumif(itemCount, status >= 500 or ((isnull(status) or status == 0) and success == false))
    by cloud_RoleName, area
| where requests >= min_requests
| extend availability_pct = round(100.0 * (requests - unavailable) / requests, 3)
| project cloud_RoleName, area, requests, availability_pct
